  "fits": [
    {
      "fact": "Choose the size by tank length. Each model covers a range from its own length up to about 10–20 cm longer, e.g. the 60 cm model fits 60–80 cm tanks.",
      "source": 0
    },
    {
      "fact": "Made for open-top tanks; the retailer says it should not run under an aquarium lid.",
      "source": 0
    },
    {
      "fact": "The legs clamp glass up to 10 mm thick on the smaller models and up to 12 mm on the 90 and 120 cm models.",
      "source": 3
    },
    {
      "fact": "Recommended for planted tanks that need strong light and full control over colour.",
      "source": 3
    },
    {
      "fact": "No UV LEDs. Hanging it takes a bulky, costly extra kit, so it is a poor choice if you want UV or a neat hanging setup.",
      "source": 3
    },
    {
      "fact": "Some users find the 60 cm model too strong for a shallow 60×36×18 cm tank and have to hang it higher or turn it down.",
      "source": 7
    }
  ],
  "usage": [
    {
      "fact": "Setup: install the My Chihiros app, put on the legs or hang the light, power it on, turn on phone Bluetooth and location, register an email, then pick the light and set the colours.",
      "source": 1
    },
    {
      "fact": "The app sets timers, preset or custom colour channels, and gradual sunrise and sunset dimming.",
      "source": 4
    },
    {
      "fact": "Keep the light at least 6 cm above the water. For indoor use only; never submerge it.",
      "source": 4
    },
    {
      "fact": "The housing gets very hot while on, so switch it off before touching it.",
      "source": 4
    },
    {
      "fact": "Unplug before cleaning or servicing. If it falls in the water, unplug at once and let it dry fully before using again.",
      "source": 4
    },
    {
      "fact": "Keep the power adapter off the tank lid. Replace damaged cables or controllers only with genuine parts.",
      "source": 4
    },
    {
      "fact": "Hobbyists advise starting at low channel levels (around 30% or less) and raising them slowly to avoid algae.",
      "source": 7
    },
    {
      "fact": "The legs adjust in length, but one buyer could not set them to the right length for a 90 cm tank, so check the fit first.",
      "source": 0
    }
  ],
  "issues": [
    {
      "fact": "It is very bright. Forum users who ran it at high channel levels got algae and had to cut the intensity.",
      "source": 8
    },
    {
      "fact": "Some owners worried the added white channel would wash out colours. Others found colours still looked good after tuning the channels.",
      "source": 8
    },
    {
      "fact": "Compared with the regular WRGB 2, the Pro adds a separate white channel, and the seller claims over 40% more light output.",
      "source": 4
    },
    {
      "fact": "Sources disagree on the 80 cm model's power: 110 W at one European retailer versus 100 W at Vietnamese shops.",
      "source": 4
    },
    {
      "fact": "A Vietnamese shop says WRGB lights render colour slightly worse than pure RGB, but the Pro has enough power to turn off the white channel.",
      "source": 3
    },
    {
      "fact": "A retailer review warns that worn drivers in used WRGB II-series lights can flicker at low brightness. This was said of the standard WRGB II, not tested on the Pro.",
      "source": 9
    },
    {
      "fact": "Mirror shades for the regular WRGB II do not fit the Pro; you need the Pro-specific shade.",
      "source": 0
    },
    {
      "fact": "Stock is patchy in Vietnam. Several shops list sizes as sold out or show conflicting stock status, and local warranty is short (1 month).",
      "source": 4
    }
  ],
  "alternatives": [
    {
      "brand": "Chihiros",
      "model": "WRGB 2 (standard)",
      "why": "Cheaper option in Vietnam (about 3.0 million ₫ for 60 cm at Thủy Sinh 4U). Slightly lower power (67 W for 60 cm) with no separate white channel; enough for most planted tanks."
    },
    {
      "brand": "Chihiros",
      "model": "WRGB II Slim",
      "why": "A lower-power, thinner model of the same WRGB II line. Suits low-tech tanks or tanks with easy plants where the Pro would be too strong."
    },
    {
      "brand": "Week Aqua",
      "model": "M Series Pro (RGB-UV)",
      "why": "Budget app-controlled RGB light with UV LEDs, which the Chihiros lacks. Costs much less abroad; check prices with Vietnamese dealers."
    }
  ],
